<title>FRANCE: CGE sees 10 pct rise in EPS from deal.</title>
<headline>CGE sees 10 pct rise in EPS from deal.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Generale des Eaux head Jean-Marie Messier said a deal announced with Havas on Thursday would boost his company's earnings per share by 10 percent in 1997.</p>
<p>He told a news conference it would give the company a net capital gain of more than two billion francs in 1997.</p>
<p>In slides shown by Messier at the news conference, the company also confirmed it was maintaining its debt reduction target of 10 to 15 billion francs by the end of 1997.</p>
</text>
